# Why: Replace upstream Documenso brand defaults at the constant layer + the
#      one consuming email template that doesn't go through the constant
#      indirection. Single source of truth so future renames are a one-file
#      constant change.
#
#      Three logical changes across two files:
#
#        1. SUPPORT_EMAIL default — upstream defaults to "support@documenso.com".
#           We flip it to "hello@pacta.ink" (the same support address used on
#           pacta.ink marketing). Env var override (NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL)
#           still works. Originally "support@bizrethink.ai" in overlay 021 v1
#           (2026-04-29); flipped to "hello@pacta.ink" in v2 (commit
#           4e0b45758, 2026-05-12) to unify with the marketing site inbox.
#
#        2. Brand constants — APP_NAME ("Pacta"), APP_PARENT_BRAND
#           ("BizRethink AI"), APP_FULL_NAME ("Pacta by BizRethink AI").
#           Downstream overlays (022 meta tags, 023 email footer, 024 route
#           copy) read these. Adding them in app.ts means future renames
#           propagate everywhere via a single constant change.
#
#        3. reset-password email template — (folded in from former phantom
#           overlay 058 on 2026-05-25 during merge prep). Two changes there:
#              a. Adds the SUPPORT_EMAIL import + replaces the hardcoded
#                 `mailto:hi@documenso.com` link with `mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`,
#                 so the brand stays consistent across the app + marketing
#                 site without per-template hardcoding.
#              b. Changes the fallback `<Img alt="Documenso Logo">` to
#                 `<Img alt="Pacta Logo">`. Pure brand rebrand for screen
#                 readers and accessibility.
#           This template is the only one in packages/email/templates/*.tsx
#           that uses a literal email address (the others go through
#           template-footer.tsx, which is patched by overlay 023). Folding
#           the change here rather than creating a tiny standalone 058
#           patch keeps all brand-rebrand surface in one reviewable place.
#
# Why-not-additive:
#   - app.ts: constants are imported by ~40+ files; can't be re-exported
#     from a separate package without breaking the existing import paths.
#     Inline patch is the only way.
#   - reset-password.tsx: the template directly renders a `<Link>` with a
#     hardcoded href. No injection point exists; the only way to swap the
#     literal is to edit the JSX.
#
# Upstream-merge-fragility: LOW.
#   - app.ts: gets ~1 commit per quarter upstream. Our changes are
#     additive (new exports) plus three line replacements; easy to
#     reapply on conflict.
#   - reset-password.tsx: upstream's biome lint reformat (className order,
#     JSX multi-line) accounts for ~80% of the diff body. Functional
#     changes are 3 small edits (import, alt text, mailto). Re-anchor
#     trivially on conflict.
#
# Discipline note — 045c piggyback:
#   The app.ts diff body also includes a `+// MODIFIED for BizRethink
#   (overlay 045c)` block adding `isBillingEnabledFromConfig` (async
#   DB-backed billing toggle). This was inlined to app.ts on 2026-05-12
#   when the admin-UI billing toggle shipped, but no patch file 045c
#   exists. It's thematically billing-async, not brand-rebrand, and
#   should live in its own overlay 045 patch.
#
#   It's included in this regenerated patch because the diff is captured
#   wholesale ("what does upstream/main differ from main today on these
#   files"). EXTRACT TO ITS OWN PATCH in the post-merge cleanup workstream.
#   When that happens, remove the corresponding hunk from this 021 patch
#   so 021 stays focused on brand.
#
# Status: REGENERATED 2026-05-25 (v3) — folds in reset-password.tsx (former
#         phantom 058) and captures the v2 SUPPORT_EMAIL change. v1 patch
#         on disk was corrupt (hunk header off-by-one) since the v2 inline
#         edit shipped without updating the patch file.

